# ─── Google AdSense ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Your publisher ID from Google AdSense dashboard.
# Format: ca-pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX  (16-digit number after "ca-pub-")
#
# Where to find it:
#   1. Log in to https://adsense.google.com
#   2. Click Account → Account information
#   3. Your Publisher ID is listed there
#
# When this variable is NOT set (e.g., in local development):
#   - The AdSense <script> tag is NOT injected into <head>
#   - All <AdUnit> components render null
#   - Zero performance impact in dev builds
#
# When this variable IS set (e.g., in production on Vercel):
#   - AdSense script loads async (non-blocking)
#   - Ad slots activate via IntersectionObserver when near viewport
#
# Vercel deployment:
#   Dashboard → Your Project → Settings → Environment Variables
#   Add: NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_ID = ca-pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
#   (set for Production environment only, not Preview/Development)
#
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_ID=ca-pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# ─── Ad Slot IDs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These are NOT env vars — they're hardcoded in src/app/page.tsx as AD_SLOTS.
# Replace the placeholder values (1111111111 etc.) with your real slot IDs.
#
# How to get slot IDs:
#   1. AdSense dashboard → Ads → By ad unit
#   2. Create new ad units or use existing ones
#   3. Copy the numeric slot ID (e.g., 9876543210)
#
# Slot mapping in page.tsx:
#   topBanner    → Between hero and resize tool  (horizontal / leaderboard)
#   postResult   → After successful download     (rectangle — highest CTR spot)
#   midContent   → Between Exam Presets section  (horizontal / in-content)
#   aboveFooter  → Just before footer            (rectangle / exit-intent)
#
